course: dictionary
lesson: 346
title: Anoint: holy oil and chosen people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anoint is a church word. In the Bible, people put holy oil on someone to bless them or to show that God had chosen them. Look at the words around it: «God sent the prophet Samuel to anoint the youngest son of Jesse, the shepherd boy David, as the future king.» The clues are prophet, God and future king, so the oil must be a sign that David was chosen.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Samuel put holy oil on David as a sign that God had chosen him as king." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Anoint also has an informal meaning. Someone can be anointed, or chosen, for an important job, with no oil at all. In «anointed as the next captain», the words captain and important job tell you that the person was chosen for a role.
fact: Anoint means to put holy oil on someone's head or body.
fact: Anointing is a sign of blessing, healing, or being chosen by God.
fact: Informally, «anointed» can mean chosen for an important role, such as «anointed as the next captain».
fact: Messiah and Christ both mean "the anointed one".
fact: A British monarch is anointed at the coronation.
exercise: «God sent the prophet Samuel to anoint the youngest son of Jesse.» What does anoint mean here? | To feed someone a meal | *To put holy oil on someone as a sign of being chosen | To hit someone gently on the head | To write a letter to someone
exercise: The team said the captain was «anointed as the next captain». What does anointed mean in this sentence? | Covered in oil from a bottle | Sick and resting in bed | Forgotten at practice | *Chosen for an important role
exercise: Which two words both mean "the anointed one"? | *Messiah and Christ | Goliath and Jesse | Samuel and David | Church and oil
test: Which word means to put holy oil on someone as a sign of blessing? | Annoy | *Anoint | Adjoin | Avoid
test: In church, oil is used at baptism, confirmation and ordination. Which word fits best? "At the service, the sick were ___ with oil." | wrapped | *anointed | painted | sneezed
exam: Which sentence uses anoint in the church sense? | The boy anointed his sandwich with jam | The cat anointed the sofa with spilled milk | *The prophet Samuel anointed David with oil to show that God had chosen him | The teacher anointed the board with chalk
